Do not start stepping physics until World Partition has finished streaming.

THE PROBLEM patch 0005 left open, in its own words: "a proper fix has to hold the vehicle until
streaming around it completes rather than racing it."

On a World Partition world the terrain streams in AROUND the vehicle, while the vehicle begins
falling on the very first physics step. If it passes the ground plane before the cells under it
activate, there is nothing to land on -- and because the streaming source follows the pawn, a
vehicle that has fallen away loads cells around its new position while the spawn unloads, so the
situation cannot recover on its own.

WHERE THE GATE GOES. PhysicsWorld's constructor takes `start_async_updator` and defaults it to
true, and initializeWorld() starts the async updator immediately -- so physics is running before
any terrain exists. ASimModeWorldBase::initializeForPlay() now passes false, and Tick() starts the
updator once UWorldPartitionSubsystem::IsStreamingCompleted() reports the world settled.

WHY UE PHYSICS IS NOT THE LEVER. This vehicle is not moved by Unreal's physics. AirSim's own
integrator writes the pose through PawnSimApi::setPose ->
pawn->SetActorLocationAndRotation(..., ETeleportType::TeleportPhysics). Disabling pawn physics
would therefore have changed nothing; the async updator is what has to be held.

WHY THE WAIT IS NON-BLOCKING. The wait lives in Tick and returns early. Blocking inside it would
stall the game thread -- which is the thread performing the streaming being waited for, so a
blocking wait would prevent the very work that ends it.

WHY THERE IS A TIMEOUT. A gate with no escape converts a race into a hang, which is a worse
failure than the one being fixed: a hang gives no diagnosis at all. After
kPhysicsGateTimeoutS the updator starts regardless and logs at Failure level that it did so,
because that is the case where the vehicle may still fall.

WORLDS WITHOUT A PARTITION ARE UNAFFECTED. isStreamingSettled() returns true when the world has
no UWorldPartitionSubsystem, so Blocks and every other non-streaming map start physics on the
first tick exactly as before.

IsStreamingCompleted(nullptr) asks the strictest form of the question -- every streaming level,
not a sphere around the vehicle. It is tried first because it needs no coordinate conversion
between AirLib NED and Unreal world space; if it proves too strict on a world whose traffic
streams continuously, the timeout still releases and the log records which path was taken.

